Planning an indoor wedding in Malaga means working inside a room that already has its own walls, chandeliers and, often, mains power your venue controls. Malaga Event Gear's [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) covers the audio visual slice of that: PA sound tuned to fill the room, an accent lighting layer on top of what the venue already has, wireless microphones and a live technician. It does not cover furniture, linens, tableware, dance floors or decor. For the full picture of what we cover for weddings, see our [wedding rentals](/blog/wedding-rentals/) overview. If you have not settled on a package yet, our [how to choose wedding rentals](/blog/how-to-choose-wedding-rentals/) guide walks through the six questions, starting with guest count, that decide between the Eco Pack and the Wedding Pack.

## Brief Overview

---

An indoor wedding raises a narrower set of AV questions than an open air one: how a PA is tuned to fill a room rather than project across open space, and how far a venue's own lighting already carries before an accent layer is worth adding. The [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) answers those with a PA sized for up to 80 guests, fairy light and warm LED accent lighting, wireless microphones and a live technician on site, for 650 euros ex VAT.

## Key Highlights

---

-   MEG's indoor wedding coverage is AV specific: room acoustics, speaker placement and lighting layered on top of the venue's own fixtures, not furniture, decor or dance floors.
-   Walls and hard surfaces reflect sound indoors, the honest inverse of open air, so an indoor PA is tuned to fill a room rather than project across a lawn or beach.
-   Indoor venues typically have more reliable mains power than a remote finca, and most do not set the amplified sound curfew a finca or villa does, though some hotel ballrooms set their own decibel limits.
-   Our fairy light and warm LED strings work as an accent layer on top of a venue's own lighting or chandeliers, not a lighting design service.

## What MEG Covers Indoors, and What It Doesn't

An indoor wedding checklist still spans furniture, catering, decor and photography, each its own vendor. MEG supplies only the audio visual slice: sound tuned for the room, wireless microphones, an accent lighting layer and, on the Wedding Pack, a live technician. Our [essential items for wedding rentals](/blog/essential-items-for-wedding-rentals/) guide covers that full list, plus wired versus wireless mic choice and ceremony versus reception sound, worth reading there rather than repeated here.

