## Conclusion

Indoor wedding AV, honestly scoped, comes down to four things: sound tuned to fill the room instead of project across open space, room size and ceiling height shaping speaker placement, an accent lighting layer on top of what the venue already has, and power that is usually more reliable indoors but still worth confirming. Malaga Event Gear's [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) covers all four for 650 euros ex VAT. For the full checklist across every wedding trade, see our [essential items for wedding rentals](/blog/essential-items-for-wedding-rentals/) guide. [Contact us](/contact/) to check availability.

## FAQs

### How does indoor wedding sound differ from outdoor?

Walls and hard surfaces reflect sound indoors, so an indoor PA is tuned to fill the room rather than project across open space the way an [outdoor PA](/blog/outdoor-wedding-rental-considerations/) has to. Ceiling height and room shape also change how sound reflects, which is why our technician places speakers for the specific room rather than one fixed layout.

### Is a live technician necessary indoors, or can I self run the sound?

For a smaller indoor ceremony, up to 50 guests, the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) is delivered, installed and tested by our crew, then run without a technician. For a larger hall, or a room whose layout only becomes clear on the day, the [Wedding Pack's](/packages/wedding/) live technician adjusts sound and lighting as the event unfolds.

### Does a room's acoustics affect microphone feedback?

Yes. A hall with hard floors and high ceilings reflects more sound back into open microphones than a carpeted room with soft furnishings, raising the risk of feedback if placement is not adjusted for the room. Our live technician manages that placement throughout the event as part of the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/).
